    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1488">

                <pb facs="1293" n="1035" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg1035"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 855.48/221</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The</hi>
                    
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State</hi>
                    
                    <hi rendition="#italic">to the Ambassador in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Gerard</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-03-25">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 25, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1423. The following telegram received from The Hague:</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>Captain steamship <hi rendition="#italic">Elfland</hi>, engaged Belgium
                        relief and flying our commission’s flag, reports his vessel attacked Sunday
                        by German aeroplane off Dutch coast. Five bombs were dropped. One struck
                        within 20 feet of ship. I have asked German Minister here to obtain
                        explanation from Berlin.</p>
                </quote>
                <p>Please bring to the attention of the German Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
